TOCCATA's own code is released under the Zero-Clause BSD license (0BSD): no
attribution, no notice preservation, no conditions.

That covers everything under main/, host/, tools/, components/audio_hal,
components/display, components/imu, components/medal_input, and the files
core/gyruss.c, core/gyruss.h, core/gyruss_internal.h, core/gyruss_video.c,
core/ay8910.c, core/ay8910.h and core/mcs48.h.

Two things carry their own licences, and one of them is contagious:

  * core/e6809.c and core/e6809.h are the 6809 CPU core from vecx, which is
    GPL-3.0. Because a build of this project links that core in, the combined
    firmware and host harness must be distributed under the terms of the
    GPL-3.0 as well. Replace that one file with a permissively licensed 6809
    and the whole project is 0BSD.
  * core/z80/ is Marat Fayzullin's Z80 emulator, which its author licenses for
    non-commercial use only.

Neither covers the game ROMs, which are not distributed here and never will be.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

